Z||000000||mikabika||10-01-2001||01:27 PM||||Anybody got a good way to change the exhaust on a 87 GT 6 engine to make it "sound" like it's got power?||||reg||5
Z||000001||skitime||10-01-2001||02:35 PM||||Straight pipe in place of the cat.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||10-01-2001||02:43 PM||||I tried the straight pipe in place of the cat before.  I didn't care for it.  I liked it at first, but after living with it, the sound became annoying.  Not too loud, I just didn't like the tone.  Perhaps some resonator tips with the cat removed would tune the sound, but that's just personal preference.  It did sound great at idle, though.  Just had a bit too much of that diesel 6 cylinder sound when coasting down through the gears. (If you've ever heard a big rig slow itself down with the engine, you know what I mean).<P>I've got a hi-flow converter on now (emissions testing in my area) and it sounds better than the original cat.  I'm thinking about going with the Spin Tech muffler from West Coast Fiero.  FieroLisa has one, but I haven't heard it yet.  I've also heard people say that replacing the cat with a glasspack is pretty good.  It gets louder, and the glasspack tunes the sound a little.  I'd recommend using a Cherry Bomb style bullet muffler (one without any fiberglass packing) so you don't have to worry about it blowing out later.||||reg||5
Z||000003||SLYGUY||10-01-2001||02:44 PM||||I like the sound of mine. It sounds best when you accelerate with about 1/2 throttle and shift smoothly at about 3700-4000rpm. Nice growl. <P>Anybody have any ideas as to why I occasionally get a small pop from the exhaust when shifting?<BR>O2 sensor?<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000004||skitime||10-01-2001||02:59 PM||||Currently, I have a cherry bomb muffler in place of the cat and I like the sound of it.  It is not as loud as the straight pipe but is a nice mellow sound.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rick 88||10-01-2001||03:21 PM||||I installed a stainless tubular resonator with a spiral inner design. It does not contain any fiberglass. The sound is slightly deeper than with the convertor. The sulfur smell went away, and the engine pulls much better above 4500 rpm. My car has also passed the emissions test for Texas, staying well within limits.<P>Rick 88||||reg||1
Z||000006||sqoach||10-01-2001||03:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLYGUY:<BR><B><BR>Anybody have any ideas as to why I occasionally get a small pop from the exhaust when shifting?<BR>O2 sensor?<P>Sly</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have the same problem. I'd also like to know.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">            <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||recluse||10-01-2001||11:22 PM||||possibly an exhaust leak?||||reg||1
Z||000008||GarethWright||10-02-2001||02:06 AM||||One of my old pals put a Flowmaster Muffler in his 280zx, that made it sound better.<BR>Then he stuck a broom handle through his cat, and poured the bits out, he said it sounded like an old Jag, I thought so too, if the Jag was on its last leg, and poorly tuned as well.<P>The Flowmasters (according to them) have less resistance, and allow for more HPs, but all I noticed was it sounded better.||||reg||1
Z||000009||GarethWright||10-02-2001||02:06 AM||||One of my old pals put a Flowmaster Muffler in his 280zx, that made it sound better.<BR>Then he stuck a broom handle through his cat, and poured the bits out, he said it sounded like an old Jag, I thought so too, if the Jag was on its last leg, and poorly tuned as well.<P>The Flowmasters (according to them) have less resistance, and allow for more HPs, but all I noticed was it sounded better.||||reg||1
