Z||000018||1FST2M6||10-04-2001||04:27 PM||||a wet nitrous system tends to puddle fuel in the exhaust if not properly tuned.. and that morning we had run it a few times painting the wall with unburnt fuel.. and apparently it was in the exhaust system too.. just an exhasut backfire.. that scared the CRAP out of me, the camera holder, the dyno tuner (Ed the guy in the car) and the 4 other people in the shop at the time. once we realized there was no falling debris we got a good laugh at everyones face the second it happend and the 10 afterwards. i'm not sure of the model # of my muffler.. i'll look on it and let ya know.. 2.5" in/out stainless packed.. it was $160 ||||reg||1
Z||000019||88Style||10-04-2001||04:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>a wet nitrous system tends to puddle fuel in the exhaust if not properly tuned.. and that morning we had run it a few times painting the wall with unburnt fuel.. and apparently it was in the exhaust system too.. just an exhasut backfire.. that scared the CRAP out of me, the camera holder, the dyno tuner (Ed the guy in the car) and the 4 other people in the shop at the time. once we realized there was no falling debris we got a good laugh at everyones face the second it happend and the 10 afterwards. i'm not sure of the model # of my muffler.. i'll look on it and let ya know.. 2.5" in/out stainless packed.. it was $160 </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That rocks! Is that muffler a crossflow style (single inlet, dual outlet with the inlet and one of the outlets on the same side?). I love the sound!! ||||reg||1
